       "body": {
        "en": "Percentages via anchors: find 10% and 1%, then build; 17% of 240 is 24 + 24 + 24 ÷ 2 + 2,4 × 2 = 40,8 <i>(Barrett, ch. 2)</i>. Fraction equivalents are often faster than decimals: 25% = ¼, 37,5% = ⅜, 12,5% = ⅛, 33,3% = ⅓. Reduce ratios by common factors before using them <i>(Barrett, Test 6)</i>. Estimate first, especially when the options are far apart. A rough answer eliminates three of five options in seconds <i>(Shavick, ch. 5)</i>. And read every word: “increase” versus “new total”; “per month” versus “per year”; “of which” versus “in addition to” <i>(Carter)</i>.",
        "id": "Hitung persentase lewat titik bantu: cari 10% dan 1%, lalu rangkai; 17% dari 240 adalah 24 + 24 + 24 ÷ 2 + 2,4 × 2 = 40,8 <i>(Barrett, bab 2)</i>. Padanan pecahan sering lebih cepat daripada desimal: 25% = ¼, 37,5% = ⅜, 12,5% = ⅛, 33,3% = ⅓. Sederhanakan perbandingan dengan faktor persekutuan sebelum dipakai <i>(Barrett, Tes 6)</i>. Perkirakan dulu, terutama kalau pilihan jawabannya berjauhan. Jawaban kasar bisa menyingkirkan tiga dari lima pilihan dalam hitungan detik <i>(Shavick, bab 5)</i>. Dan baca setiap katanya: “kenaikan” atau “total baru”; “per bulan” atau “per tahun”; “di antaranya” atau “ditambah” <i>(Carter)</i>."
       },
